      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "We can set up a proportion to solve this problem. Let \\( x \\) be the number of minutes it takes to print 200 pages. The equation we need to solve is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{17 \\text{ pages}}{1 \\text{ minute}} = \\frac{200 \\text{ pages}}{x \\text{ minutes}}\n\\]\n\nCross-multiplying gives:\n\n\\[\n17x = 200\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{200}{17} \\approx 11.7647\n\\]\n\nRounding to the nearest whole number, we get:\n\n\\[\nx \\approx 12\n\\]\n\nSo, it will take approximately 12 minutes to print 200 pages. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given values\r\npages_per_minute = 17\r\ntotal_pages = 200\r\n\r\n# Calculate the time in minutes to print 200 pages\r\nminutes = total_pages / pages_per_minute\r\nminutes_rounded = round(minutes)\r\n\r\nprint(minutes_rounded)\n```\n```output\n12\n```\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).",
